WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 line:92%
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're here
with Secretary Buttigieg.

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:06.539
You are unabashed about the fact
that you love transportation

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:09.509 size:78% position:39%
and I agree with you,
that I think that,

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
travel is very romantic.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
With that said,
I've spent a lot of time

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the O'Hare Airport
over the years,

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:17.484 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and I never thought

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
it would be a place
where I would want to propose,

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.554 size:75% position:38%
but that is, indeed,
where you proposed

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.455 line:92%
to your husband, at O'Hare

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughing ]
What was it about O'Hare?

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I know
not everybody understands

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
that O'Hare
can be a romantic place,

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
but it absolutely can.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, the first time
Chaston and I ever communicate

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.134 line:92%
was on this app called Hinge

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:38.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was sitting at Gate B
at the airport.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.239 line:92%
He had a job that involved

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:42.275
helping exchange students
move through the airport.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:45.612
And I always remembered that
in a certain technical sense

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:48.114
even though it was remotely,
that was where we first met.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:51.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, later on, when the tim
came to propose,

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
I found this app
I could check on

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:55.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it was going
to be quiet at that gate,

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.190 size:88% position:44%
based on when the planes
were coming and going,

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were taking
a vacation that day,

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I kind of guided him
into that spot.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.097 size:81% position:41%
I was like, you know,
"Why don't you show me

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
that spot
where you first were

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:08.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we first started
chatting with each other?"

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, just behind, there wa
a little bit of space

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:13.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
behind that gate agent
stand in the window

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:18.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I invited him to look
out the window there

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.279 line:92%
and then got on one knee.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.182
I told him it'd be, you know
a lot like being in the airport.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:25.985
Life with me would be probably
hard to steal private moments,

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.654 line:92%
but also full of adventure

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:30.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, luckily for me,
he said yes.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
And, considering

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
how many divorces
have started in O'Hare,

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I think it's nice that there's

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.831 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at least one

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:40.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughing ] story
about a marriage starting.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.736 line:92%
You know, I think one of the -

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:44.737 line:92%
I should note, by the way,

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had no sense
of what the logo was

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the Department
of Transportation

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.779 line:92%
and I'm noticing it behind you

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.247 line:92%
I feel like, I don't know,

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:55.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
it could be
a little more romantic

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
than what you guys
are doing right there.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.653
Just put that very much
at the back of your list,

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
but let's get something
a little flashier.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Alright. I'll Look into it.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.894 line:92%
-It seems like maybe the job

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:10.196
and the people who've had th
job before you over the year

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.664 size:84% position:42% line:92%
have focused on things,

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe primarily
on automobile travel.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.202 line:92%
It does seem like there is

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
a shift happening
in this country,

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:21.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, cities
having more bike lanes,

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.076 line:92%
having more pedestrian walkways.

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.644 line:92%
Is that something that you fee

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:27.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
is very much
under your purview as well

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and this is
really important to get righ

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
for safety reasons,
climate reasons,

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:31.885 line:92%
and a lot of other reasons

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:36.289
You know, there's this old ide
that roads are just for cars

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:38.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
I believe roads are
for human beings

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:41.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
and human beings might be
in a car

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.428 size:88% position:44% line:92%
or might be on a bicycle

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
or a scooter
or on foot or in a wheelchair,

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
and roads need
to support everybody,

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
however it is
that you get around.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.471
That was a really importan
principle for how we improve

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of roadways
in the city of South Bend

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I was mayor,
and I think it's something

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
that our department
ought to support.

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:58.978 line:92%
You know, the reality is that --

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's this idea called
complete streets,

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.448
but it's about something
even more simple than that

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:05.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is just safe streets
and sometimes the safest stree

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:09.556
or the best street is not on
that's just about shooting car

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:12.058
through the middle of
a community as fast as possible.

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's about making sure
people can get

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
to where they need to go,
safely,

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.131
and making sure that our streets
are vibrant

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:19.832 line:92%
and support us in our lives.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.533 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And I think all of us,

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:23.036
especially as we've been
in this pandemic reality,

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
have had occasion to think
in new ways

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
about just how much
it means to us

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:31.077
to be in those shared spaces
which is what our streets are.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:33.513
-It seems like there's
a lot of discussion, now,

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:36.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
about sort of high-tech,
futuristic solutions

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.618 size:75% position:38% line:92%
to transportation --

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:42.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
super fast tubes
or autonomous vehicles.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:46.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you both embrace
the possibilities of those

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
while not losing focus
on the fact that

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
most people,
certainly in cities,

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:53.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
would just like working buses,
working subways?

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:57.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Right.
I mean, before we talk

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
about some of these
really exciting technologies

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've got to take care
of the basics.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.643
Don't get me wrong --
the technologies are compelling.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.345 size:81% position:41%
They're fascinating.
There's a lot going on

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:08.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
with drones delivering
packages right now.

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:11.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've got to learn how to deal
with this, as a country --

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.553 line:92%
automated vehicles, hyperloops

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
magnetic levitation,
you name it.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:16.389 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But, as a mayor,

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also think a lot about thing
like filling potholes,

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:21.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
making sure that our bridges
are in good shape.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, because this country,
unfortunately,

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
has systematically failed
to invest

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a very long time,
we're behind.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:32.105
So, if we want to have the bes
infrastructure in the world,

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
if America wants to lead
the world

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:38.878
and not be just another country,
then we've got to fix it first

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
Fix it first,
and be looking ahead

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:44.550
to these future technologies
that are coming, ready or not.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The present that we're living
in right now, obviously,

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
due to situations
outside the control

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the Department
of Transportation,

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:55.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
has more -- I should say,
has less commuters

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:57.363 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
than maybe any time

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:58.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, certainly,
the last 50 years.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
How does that affect
how you look to the future

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
not knowing how long
working remotely

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:09.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
is going to be a part of the
American work experience?

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:10.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
I think the next normal

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:12.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
is not going to be
like the last one

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:15.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we don't yet know
everything that that means

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:18.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think, for a lot of employer
and a lot of workers,

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:21.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
the 9 to 5
will never quite be the same

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's safe
to say all of us are ready

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
to not be on Zoom,
not be online,

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
quite as often as we are,
but that doesn't mean

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're going to snap right back
to the old patterns,

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:33.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that means how people
commute might change,

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.167 line:92%
real estate might change,

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
the way we use our land
might change.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:39.339
And the reality is there's
no predicting that just yet.

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:40.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just got to make sure
we're flexible

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:44.844
and ready to return to something
better than what we had before

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I really appreciate
your time.

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
Best of luck with all of i
moving forward.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
Secretary Pete Buttigieg,
everybody.

